\section{Liquidity and capacity}\label{sec:liq}
v2 holds its OOS edge up to << V('cap.1x.oos.capital') >> of capital (5\(\times\) loses), trading
<< V('v2.is.share_vol') >> of match volume; the CV book's Sharpe halves at
<< V('capcv.half.oos') >>--<< V('capcv.half.is') >> post hoc (Fig.~\ref{fig:capacity}), and pre-registered it has no
capacity. Price impact, fitted on << V('liq.orders.fit') >> IS taker orders with a usable mid, grows with the log of
size (<< V('liq.temp.top.small') >>¢ a share at 1--10 shares, << V('liq.temp.top.large') >>¢ at 10,000+ in the
highest-volume fifth), the mid moves << V('liq.lambda30') >>¢ more per 1,000 shares at 30\,s (less on burned-OOS
tapes: the fit is unstable), and in four hours of live book, buying just after a reprice cost << V('liq.M') >> times a
quiet book. With that charged, v2's Sharpe still halves near << V('liq.v2.half.oos.central') >> OOS, but 1\(\times\)
earns << V('liq.v2.1x.oos.central') >> a day, not << V('liq.v2.1x.oos.none') >> (<< V('liq.v2.1x.oos.cons') >>
conservatively, interval << V('liq.v2.1x.oos.cons.ci') >>); CV capacity moves under << V('liq.cv.half.move') >>.
Taking half the stale depth is cautious: in << V('liq.l2.reprices') >> live reprices and << V('liq.phi.official') >>
stamped points, other takers took << V('liq.phi.took') >> of it. COURTSIDE prices speed; it is not yet a business.

% ======================================================================================== 8 Limitations
\section{Limitations and next steps}\label{sec:limits}
The stamp lag \(L\) is unmeasured and moves the break-even one for one; trading is simulated, the vision is tested on
other matches and the fresh holdout is two days. A fee rise, a shorter hold or more fast wallets would break the edge.
Next: a week of licensed feed to measure \(L\), the forward test, and the limits in the live engine.\label{lastmain}

